    "reason": "The source-backed wrong transformation in PR #136650/#135709 is the pre-fix lowering of length extraction through `PtrMetadata` of a reborrow (plus `FakeRead(ForIndex)` + constant for arrays), with borrowck classifying it as `Shallow(None)` instead of `Shallow(Some(ArtificialField::ArrayLength))`. This is runtime-value-equivalent: it reads the same length metadata (or the same static array length) as restored `Rvalue::Len(place)`. The actual regression demonstrated by the PR is compile-time borrowck rejection of disjoint element/field borrows (`tests/ui/borrowck/array-disjoint-borrows-issue-135671.rs` is `//@ check-pass`), not a changed runtime result. The harness requires two Rust functions that both pass Miri and produce deterministic different values on the same inputs; no such pair exists for this transformation without fabricating an unrelated semantic change. The paired array/slice length computations agree on every concrete input, and the incorrect behavior (rejecting valid code) cannot be observed as a Miri-passing runtime value difference.",
    "evidence": [],
